```mdl
verdict SyncLinearTeams: Pull-then-push per bound team works, but the input and error shapes differ from the spec.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-linear/src/types/LinearOperation.ts#SyncLinearTeams, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-linear/src/operations/sync.ts#syncTeamBinding, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-linear/src/operations/sync.ts#pushTeamUpdates, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-connector/src/Binding.ts#syncAll]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-linear/src/operations/sync.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The operation takes the connection and an optional priority cursor id. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-linear/src/types/LinearOperation.ts#SyncLinearTeams
    - Binding.syncAll fans out over every external cursor of the connection, isolating failures. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-connector/src/Binding.ts#syncAll
    - syncTeamBinding pulls projects, milestones and issues, pushes divergences, records the cursor outcome and toasts. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-linear/src/operations/sync.ts#syncTeamBinding
    - pushTeamUpdates diffs each mirrored object against its snapshot and patches Linear. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-linear/src/operations/sync.ts#pushTeamUpdates
  note: |
    The input has `priority?: string` (a cursor id to sync first) instead of `team?: Ref<Project>`. A missing database fails
    with `ConnectorSync.DatabaseMissingError`, not `IntegrationDatabaseMissing`, and an unbound team adds
    `LinearTeamUnresolvedError`. Projects mirror as `TaskSet`, and milestones are pulled too.
```

